articles.content_en:
Litigation cases related to the regulatory functions of a stock exchange include:
(1) actions arising from handling decisions made by a stock exchange in accordance with the provisions of the Company Law of the People's Republic of China, the Securities Law of the People's Republic of China, the Securities Investment Fund Law of the People's Republic of China, the Measures for the Administration of Stock Exchanges and other laws, regulations and rules, with respect to securities issuers and their relevant personnel, stock exchange members and their relevant personnel, and securities listing and trading activities;
(2) actions arising from handling decisions made by a stock exchange in accordance with the lawful authorization of the securities regulatory authority under the State Council, with respect to securities issuers and their relevant personnel, stock exchange members and their relevant personnel, and securities listing and trading activities;
(3) actions arising from handling decisions made by a stock exchange in accordance with the provisions of its articles of association, business rules and business contracts, with respect to securities issuers and their relevant personnel, stock exchange members and their relevant personnel, and securities listing and trading activities;
(4) other actions arising in the course of a stock exchange's performance of its regulatory functions.
